        "concept": "CellStructure",
        "key_terms": ["organelles", "organized structure", "parts", "jobs", "heart", "lungs", "functions"],
        "source_span": "Even though a cell is small, it has an organized structure. Inside a cell there are many different parts, and each part has its own job to do. These parts are called organelles. Just like the organs in your body each have a function \u2014 your heart pumps blood, your lungs help you breathe \u2014 the organelles inside a cell each perform a specific function that keeps the cell alive and working properly."
    },
    {
        "concept": "CellMembrane",
        "key_terms": ["thin outer layer", "surrounds", "protect", "control substances"],
        "source_span": "Three important parts found inside cells are: - **The cell membrane.** This is the thin outer layer that surrounds the cell. Its job is to protect the cell and to control what substances are allowed to enter or leave."
    },
    {
        "concept": "Nucleus",
        "key_terms": ["control center", "instructions", "cell functions"],
        "source_span": "- **The nucleus.** This is often called the control center of the cell, because it contains the instructions that direct everything the cell does."
    },
    {
        "concept": "Cytoplasm",
        "key_terms": ["jelly-like substance", "fills", "organelles", "float"],
        "source_span": "- **The cytoplasm.** This is the jelly-like substance that fills the inside of the cell. The other organelles float inside the cytoplasm."
    },
